  "ethanol feed 1.0 mol/s anhydrous at 25 C; the plant runs at about 1.5 bar in the reactor section (no pressure stated)",
  "E1 feed/effluent exchanger: feed heated to 80 C (liquid, just below its boiling point at 1.5 bar); the effluent side removes the same duty (tied by a Spec block)",
  "vaporiser outlet = reactor temperature 230 C (document: superheated vapour; reactor 200-260 C)",
  "reactor isothermal at 230 C (fixed bed with the stated 200-260 C window; the document calls it endothermic and equilibrium limited, so the duty is reported); a 0.5 % ethanol side conversion to diethyl ether gives the light end the first column removes",
  "water-cooled condenser outlet 35 C",
  "5 % of the hydrogen goes to the hydrogenation step, 95 % is exported (document: 'partly compressed')",
  "hydrogenation at 5 bar (no pressure stated)",
  "D1 first column: 12 stages, total condenser (the dissolved hydrogen is purged ahead of it), feed stage 6, 1.5 bar top, reflux ratio 3; liquid distillate = ether + acetaldehyde left + 2 % of the ester",
  "pressure-swing pair D2/D3: 99 % of the ethanol and water to the recycle, 1 % of the ester with it; specified, not simulated (the document gives no pressures and does not say which column takes the feed)",
  "D4 product column: 10 stages, total condenser, 1 atm, reflux ratio 2, bottoms purge 1 % of the feed (no heavy compound exists in the basis, so the purge is ester)"
